 "id": "cases/transport-iter-15ma",
 "type": "fyo:ScenarioSpecification",
 "title": {
  "zh": "ITER 15 MA 的剖面（固定几何、单通道、定态）",
  "en": "ITER 15 MA cross-section (fixed geometry, one channel, steady state)"
 },
 "note": {
  "zh": "★这一档与含时演化栏那一档<strong>同源</strong>（2026-08-24 随那一档的形状与 χ₀ 一起改过：κ 1.70→1.86、δ 0.34→0.48、χ₀ 0.6→0.40，理由见那一档的说明与 `docs/note/fuse-cases.md` §5）：装置尺寸（a = 2.0 m、R/a = 3.1、κ = 1.86、δ = 0.48、B<sub>0</sub> = 5.3 T、n<sub>e</sub>(0) = 10×10<sup>19</sup> m<sup>-3</sup>、χ₀ = 0.40 m²/s）是两条栏<strong>共读</strong>的那一组，所以两边必须写同一个数——同一台机器在两条栏上是两个数，比没有预设更坏。★<strong>这一栏答的不是同一个问题</strong>：它解「给定这套规矩与这一个 χ，剖面长什么样」，<strong>报不出</strong> W<sub>th</sub>、τ<sub>E</sub>、β<sub>N</sub>、Q——那些在含时演化栏里。加热源峰值是<strong>任意单位</strong>的温度变化率，不是 MW。★边界值 3 keV 是台基顶（与含时演化栏那一档同一个数，出处见 <code>docs/note/iter-15ma-benchmark.md</code> §3：ASTRA 的参考剖面恰在 x = 0.948 处过 3.008 keV）。",
  "en": "★<strong>Same numbers as the time-dependent bar's ITER case</strong>: the machine sizes (a = 2.0 m, R/a = 3.1, κ = 1.70, δ = 0.34, B<sub>0</sub> = 5.3 T, n<sub>e</sub>(0) = 10×10<sup>19</sup> m<sup>-3</sup>, χ₀ = 0.40 m²/s) are the group the two bars <strong>share</strong>, so both must say the same thing — one machine reading as two numbers on two bars is worse than no preset at all. ★<strong>This bar answers a different question</strong>: given these rules and this one χ, what does the profile look like. It <strong>cannot report</strong> W<sub>th</sub>, τ<sub>E</sub>, β<sub>N</sub> or Q — those live on the time-dependent bar. The source peak is a temperature rate in <strong>arbitrary units</strong>, not MW. ★The 3 keV boundary is the pedestal top, the same number the other bar's ITER case uses (provenance in <code>docs/note/iter-15ma-benchmark.md</code> §3: the ASTRA reference profile passes 3.008 keV at x = 0.948)."
 },
 "prescribed_task_kind": "fyo:PhysicsModelingTask",
 "prescribes_code": {
  "id": "code/transport",
  "type": "spo:Code",
  "name": "fylite",
  "comment": "capability `transport` of the fylite tool register (python/fylite/scenario/__init__.py TOOLS['transport']); the parameter IRIs `code/transport#<name>` are this capability's control vocabulary"
 },
